{"name":"Silver Bullet","hex":"#b6b5b8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver bullet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bullet made of silver, usually with reference to the folkloric belief that such bullets are the only weapons which can kill a werewolf, vampire, or other monster.","Any straightforward solution perceived to have great effectiveness or to bring miraculous results."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver_bullet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver bullet","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a silver bullet is often one of the few weapons that are effective against a werewolf, vampire, witch, or other supernatural being."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Lone_Ranger_Silver_Bullet.jpg/330px-Lone_Ranger_Silver_Bullet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_bullet","wikidata":"Q841402"},{"title":"The Silver Bullet (1935 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Silver Bullet is a 1935 American Western film directed by Bernard B. Ray and starring Tom Tyler, Jayne Regan and Lafe McKee."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3f/The_Silver_Bullet_%28film%29.jpg/330px-The_Silver_Bullet_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Silver_Bullet_(1935_film)","wikidata":"Q55635544"},{"title":"Silver Bullet (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver Bullet is a 1985 American horror film based on the 1983 Stephen King novella Cycle of the Werewolf. It stars Gary Busey, Everett McGill, and Corey Haim, with Megan Follows, Terry O'Quinn, Lawrence Tierney, Bill Smitrovich, Kent Broadhurst, David Hart, and James Gammon in supporting roles. The film is directed by Dan Attias, written by King and produced by Martha De Laurentiis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Silver_bullet_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Bullet_(film)","wikidata":"Q1198033"},{"title":"Bullet","blocks":[{"text":"A bullet is a type of projectile that is shot from the barrel of a firearm. Bullets are made of a variety of materials, including copper, lead, steel, polymer, rubber and even wax. They do not normally contain explosives, but are kinetic projectiles that strike or damage the target by transferring kinetic energy upon impact and penetration. They are made in shapes and constructions that vary for different applications, including specialized functions such as hunting, target shooting, combat, and training. They are often tapered, making them more aerodynamic. Bullet size is expressed by weight and diameter in both imperial and metric measurement systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/GP11_coupe.JPG/330px-GP11_coupe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bullet","wikidata":"Q174583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/MaryRose-round_shot.JPG/500px-MaryRose-round_shot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/MaryRose-round_shot.JPG/1280px-MaryRose-round_shot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/MaryRose-round_shot.JPG/500px-MaryRose-round_shot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Round shot from the 16th century Mary Rose English warship, showing both stone and iron ball shot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaryRose-round_shot.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Naseby_musket_balls.jpg/500px-Naseby_musket_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p